From f2e4a72037d9c17a0a50686fdfe8f3a205eec3f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:37:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 187/187] media: s5p-mfc: decode the first H.263 picture

H.263 has no header of its own: the picture header of the first frame
is what SEQ_START parses, as with VP8. Decode that buffer rather than
completing it unused, which lost the first picture and left every
picture up to the next intra one predicted from an empty reference.

Tested on Exynos7870 with Android's Codec2 V4L2 decoder: H.263 QCIF and
CIF decoded identical to ffmpeg, first picture included.

---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
index 9f47ef9dd7..5c9c8ac55a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
@@ -604,11 +604,14 @@ static void s5p_mfc_handle_seq_done(struct s5p_mfc_ctx *ctx,
 				ctx->head_processed = 0;
 			else
 				ctx->head_processed = 1;
-		} else if (ctx->codec_mode == S5P_MFC_CODEC_VP8_DEC) {
+		} else if (ctx->codec_mode == S5P_MFC_CODEC_VP8_DEC ||
+			   ctx->codec_mode == S5P_MFC_CODEC_H263_DEC) {
 			/*
 			 * The buffer that carried the header is the first key
 			 * frame: decode it, rather than completing it unused and
 			 * decoding the next frames against an empty reference.
+			 * H.263 has no header of its own either: the picture
+			 * header of the first frame is the one parsed.
 			 */
 			ctx->head_processed = 0;
 		} else {
